                    briefing_text_r1:       `Day one of the mandate. You hold Liwanag’s P&L, the supply-risk analysis, the farmer-income data and the customer’s ESG ultimatum. For decades the firm ran a <strong>foundation</strong> — scholarships and relief — entirely separate from operations. It generates goodwill but <em>no competitive advantage and no supply security</em>. Diagnose <em>why</em> disconnected philanthropy fails, map where social impact and business value could be <strong>co-created</strong> in the value chain, and define what “institutionalize” concretely means — strategy, structure, incentives — not a bigger foundation.`,
